Downloaded at build time (not in the source tarball)
-----------------------------------------------------

Reference-LAPACK 3.12.1 (https://github.com/Reference-LAPACK/lapack,
license of LAPACK as above, LICENSE section 6):

  - interfaces/lapack/reference/fetch.sh downloads it (checksum verified)
    for libulmlapack (interfaces/install-shared.sh with a Fortran
    compiler) and for the LAPACK test programs
    (test/reference-lapack.sh, test/reference-lapack-lin.sh).
  - libulmlapack is Reference-LAPACK compiled on top of libulmblas: a
    package that ships it must also ship the LAPACK license (LICENSE
    section 6).  The distribution recipes in packaging/ build with
    FC=none and do not ship libulmlapack (except the Homebrew tap,
    packaging/homebrew).

Runtime libraries linked statically
------------------------------------

On Linux and Windows the shared libraries link the C++ runtime
(libstdc++) and libgcc statically by default (Windows also winpthread).
These are licensed under the GPL (GNU General Public License; GNU: GNU's
Not Unix) version 3 with the GCC (GNU Compiler Collection) Runtime Library Exception 3.1,
which allows this without conditions on ulmBLAS; winpthread (MinGW-w64)
is under the MIT (Massachusetts Institute of Technology) and BSD 3-Clause
licenses.  ULMBLAS_STATIC_LIBSTDCXX=no
links libstdc++ dynamically (distribution packages).

Git repository only (not in the release tarballs)
--------------------------------------------------

The benchmark programs (bench/, with files of ATLAS, the Automatically
Tuned Linear Algebra Software, LICENSE section 5) and the reference BLAS
for benchmarks (refblas/, LICENSE section 6) are in the Git repository
but not in the release tarballs (.gitattributes, export-ignore).
